    A-3.21 fixup4: free p2_shrunk in T12 cleanup (memory leak fix)
    
    Fixes Steward's finding: p2_shrunk was allocated by T12.5's allocator
    (which moved from p2_new) but never freed in cleanup. p2_new was already
    freed by the allocator during the move, so only p2_shrunk needed freeing.
    
    Ownership table now documented in cleanup:
      p_new      — alive, tracked → untrack + free
      p2_new     — freed by T12.5 allocator → DO NOT free (avoid double-free)
      p2_shrunk  — alive, tracked → untrack + free  [fixup4: was leaked]
      p_inplace  — same as p_inplace_base → untrack + free once
    
    Results: 133 tests, exit 0. TSan: 0 races.

